# ---------------------------------------------------------------- private
# Everything here belongs to whoever is running the app, not to the project.
#
# cache/ is the big one: it holds the Spotify OAuth token, the four Chrome
# profiles (with their cookies and saved logins), downloaded album art, the
# lyrics cache and any images dragged in. None of it should ever be committed.
music-deck/cache/
cache/

# Written on first run, next to whichever copy of the app you started - so it
# turns up in dist/ as well as here. Music folder paths and the Spotify client id.
config.json

# Belt and braces, in case any of these ever appear.
*.token.json
spotify_token.json
.env
*.pem
*.key

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- build
# The throwaway PyInstaller virtualenv and its scratch space.
.build-env/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.spec

# dist/ is deliberately NOT ignored - the built .exe living in the repo is how
# this gets handed to people.
